        "source_clause_hashes": [
          {
            "sha256": "1f013308a12fc6fd66b3b7821cfdbdc488de218eabe57b5c7c93fe9a22e3fa09",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "Use this capability to perform a read-only structural health audit of an existing codebase. It measures codebase risk through concrete metrics, verifies prior audit claims against live files, detects drift between audit snapshots, and produces slice-ready remediation recommendations."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "d69fe723b3887def45dca57abfef8166fafcde3dbc66c808c8ad8e0dec58c039",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "This is a direct skill surface, not an autonomous agent. It may read files, list directories, inspect symbols, and search references. It must not modify, create, delete, stage, commit, install dependencies, run tests, or deploy anything in the target codebase."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "2d9f614a2daa074ad5340d050d26e2ca590b858c3df44039d6f812ba63ebad89",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "`cruft_inventory` is a distinct optional mode. It requires Bash plus Python 3.11 or newer. Enter it only when the user explicitly asks to scan the configured home-level agent-tool locations; do not infer it from a repository health request, do not traverse arbitrary home paths, and do not merge its results into the target-repository audit unless the user asks. In this mode, use the bundled resource to inventory generated, backup, or temporary-file sprawl:"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "209de507b86718df20faab51846e4fd8edf3be9cb7ead334daa4c4f367e99a4f",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "The authored wrapper and its Python helper are intentionally mode 644; invoke the wrapper through Bash. Default report mode is read-only and emits either a human table or one JSON object. Diagnostics go to stderr."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "7eaea818bbf8727739d263a1f8e87fb94188d078343889a50f575eafd5d4e485",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "The audit stops after the preview and never invokes `--confirm`. Actual Trash moves are outside this capability and require a separately authorized operator workflow. The standalone tool requires `--confirm` plus the exact `--expect-sha256` digest emitted by the reviewed dry-run; it rejects additions, removals, replacements, or metadata/content changes in the selected set. Never infer cleanup authority, never prompt on a TTY, and never widen the category."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "276dd992b40c532985fbd1cf72d03b0ed836b4fea7293dc98818b7d34a9a903b",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "Exit codes are `0` success/no-op, `1` unexpected internal failure, `2` usage, `3` unavailable environment dependency, `4` explicit confirmation or reviewed digest required, `5` one or more Trash moves failed, and `6` stale selection."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "e3449c878c05d744334f9aa7af2d8aa02e73dd31297b37bb6abe3489e981c93b",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "- read-only inventory of known generated, backup, and temporary-file categories"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "cc7e75cac40682cb7593c56064ee9394e362c350793f92da8108bcaccebe4766",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "- produce a read-only brownfield health report"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "0885e217a2ed838c3caa07eb501cd20465206c8cb258fe17ad73d196015c2d5d",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "## READ-ONLY MODE (Non-Negotiable)"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "54683e0251043ba51e2c63472e388de8cf1c0b0b0c8a62e886726872e33bfdd8",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "You MUST NOT modify, create, or delete any files in the target codebase. You are a read-only analyst. Any file-write attempt is a skill violation."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "77357dbdaba34183181a2940a8cdce735aae457d5f4694b620c0fe81799c73b6",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "## Required Inputs"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "3c173ef642adcc0e4bc30af8528440bc87a3edec1c72ad9d6d64acaa535078ef",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "- cruft inventory: `mode: cruft_inventory` plus an explicit request to scan the fixed home-level agent-tool categories; no repository target is required."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "882ae0abbe84e71dd35fb14defca06bf63b3c12232051b0fdfd5efecfb15db16",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "1. **Target path** (required) \u2014 Root directory of the codebase to analyze."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "378f44d68babd5603f1913f66b98afe173ed03ba02dd40fbfedc206db1350760",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "# Target (required)"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "e77e9c49f191e08f17554be0cfabdb5b529aa1840d87f8f9df5fb39634f22ca4",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "- Must have `timestamp` (ISO 8601)"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "24cae4235ef6ca00a7c3388eb226022f069b44d72e20f73c5215b9fa19f672bc",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "- Must have `findings` (list, may be empty)"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "d0ebc5bf0cfe27a3d195db775e018f44be95296af2beb89c115dc36076c9b88d",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "- Each finding must have: `id`, `category`, `severity`, `file_path`, `evidence`"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "49cfdb7532554776d0b528844c7a3628cfde52afbf5b05f494e9751dafcc95d6",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "Run these sub-phases. For each, scan only files matching `languages` config and not matching `exclude_patterns`."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "14d27afbed8a1c6ef5f6969969bfcac5ef78ae81a75312636992b9f509efb716",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "- `medium` confidence: only referenced in tests (possibly test-only utility)"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "5dbf3373cc3eca7daf4925bc64525cc602b6458a96f5c56f76cf0b32d424ae31",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "- `low` confidence: referenced only in strings/comments (dynamic dispatch possible)"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "82a950be68b15972827c701c01a36572b742de8f132e5e16190db2f5487ff045",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "3. Filter by `dead_code_confidence_floor` config \u2014 only report findings at or above this level."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "3d4b9f171064970a2e9947e6e3f0fb13501d9ced9a9ac9ebe2cde123882829ec",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "## Required Output"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "77f58a436a960bf778f726b1cbc724dc2b61f3b01800df59ced7af039ee90293",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "trajectory:  # only present if prior_state provided"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "13bd277404e79960bb0a5157a4bd6c869022c4bebb35e73cfdb09c7927236cd6",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "*Only present when prior_state is provided.*"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "13bd277404e79960bb0a5157a4bd6c869022c4bebb35e73cfdb09c7927236cd6",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "*Only present when prior_state is provided.*"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "59c80a92975d26c6e763498120b0cd5f58e7491d0ffc11900dfa57e8b154df48",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "**Trajectory:** degrading \u2014 3 new findings and 1 worsened vs only 1 resolved."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "c64a24006f7b2703ebc01885718e063d81ef98d835239a88c5a37622b3524301",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "- read-only scan of matching files only"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "6e7b14ee84cec870bc1ec5d30ea8a3ae14fa7992268674e923a076581858ecaf",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "| Read-only safety | The audit never modifies files, runs tests, installs dependencies, stages changes, commits, or deploys |"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "3185b2c8579672e73d79697e380c37aef30b3a8e426502ef97d4c3fa1435dc1b",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "4. **Monorepo:** Analyze only the subtree at `target`. Do not traverse parent directories."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "f7f2a39173d968e1630542ba7544afc6dfc2d4df78d05b0be5a840c3b6cce327",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "- **Read-only.** Never modify, create, or delete files in the target."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "ec47980ffc2e3615f42aaab11e8aee6d30b6711b2dbd082f005eb2dfd7f87b49",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "- **Scoped.** Only analyze files matching `languages` config. Skip everything else."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "6cd8b78d112144317fb67db7d9d1cd064cc6683c232329f531bb60bb9e0649b0",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "- **Non-interactive.** Bundled tools take flags, provide `--help` and `--json`, and never wait for TTY input."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "495ab00fe4ccdf0906a036810e9057ef39860cd82a69092212252a019cefa1c4",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "- **Allowed:** Read files, grep/search, count lines, inspect AST/symbols, list directories; in explicit `cruft_inventory` mode, invoke the bundled reporter only in report or dry-run mode."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "db8e49467720840db501582ff5cce010117bfb6a997dc2b9271ec2c7e43f47cd",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "- **Forbidden:** Write files, run target/application code, install dependencies, execute tests, modify git state. The only executable exception is the bundled reporter in explicit `cruft_inventory` report or dry-run mode."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "fac7308fc753e7364810b482102da1e7e819381425febf8aedd509d7ef140b6b",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "Existing domain checks, source rules, uncertainty labels, required artifact contents and permission boundaries remain mandatory. Producing an artifact includes its domain observations or findings; the independent review findings below are a separate list of defects in that artifact. Required output formats apply to the writer's artifact, not coordinator dispatches or reviewer findings. Completing an author checklist or assigning an author score does not accept the artifact. This review does not replace another workflow's approval, identity, path-fit or bounded return protocol, and grants no wider execution authority."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "283e7be539f472b9be3611179d19aa6dcb47a7d6be2764415c7e007a45e1dd1d",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "- **Writer**: writes the artifact only and repairs it from the review findings. Resume the same writer for every revision; do not start a fresh writer for a revision."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "dea1be25a70cb9c3b76aec16b97d9fbc43e09d315850ca53a095b5979399cdeb",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "- **Reviewer**: did not write the artifact, checks claims against the sources and retained domain rules, and writes findings only. The reviewer does not rewrite the artifact. Resume the same reviewer for every later round."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "32659bf6e33c011c3144f25db8d302cc6162072c987fd8cf23e4b4a1c5b5a84c",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "Use actual separate participants. If they or their resumed contexts are unavailable, report required review as incomplete; do not substitute self-review, coordinator authorship or simulated roles. Each participant stays within the existing allowed reads, writes and checks."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "420f35be46a1e2897db9a15706174ebb232e5c4ec39ec538a64eeab0e9adfe80",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "2. The coordinator dispatches the current artifact, original task and sources to the separate reviewer. The reviewer is hostile in the ordinary sense: verify each material claim, cite the source, and do not invent a defect to fill a section. Unsupported claims, misleading certainty or omitted required uncertainty warrant source-grounded findings; a clearly labeled permitted gap is not itself proof of a defect."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "ddb7354cd7f77d788c2dbbbe162d7d65f9699f0123127b140402db5149370349",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "4. The coordinator returns every open finding to the same writer. The writer repairs the artifact and responds to each received identifier with `addressed` and what changed, `wontfix` and a technical reason, or `needs-user-input` when only a human can choose. These are repair dispositions, not authored review findings or acceptance decisions. Findings awaiting a human answer remain unresolved."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "ee18a182fff070e270d8848d35b7ce527647fed86ac15c70c9814cdb3ca9e93d",
            "source": "ssot/engos-audit-code-health.md",
            "text": "6. The coordinator counts the reviewer's current open findings and resumes the same writer and reviewer until the reviewer explicitly reports zero open findings on the current artifact. There is no round cap. Do not finalize while any finding is open, while a required human answer is pending or while required review is incomplete. The inner finding count does not decide acceptance by a wider workflow."
          }
        ],
        "review_status": "draft"
      },
