        "editable_behavior": [],
        "primary_outcome": {
          "metric": "skill_specific_task_success",
          "definition": "Canonical task success with protected behavior preserved.",
          "threshold": "human_review_required"
        },
        "secondary_outcomes": [],
        "regression_limits": {
          "protected_binary_margin": 0.02,
          "critical_deterministic": "exact_pass"
        },
        "cost_latency_limits": {
          "profile_caps": {
            "static": 0,
            "native": 0,
            "routing-canary": 300000,
            "canary": 1250000,
            "promotion": 5000000,
            "cross-host": 12000000,
            "sweep": 30000000
          }
        },
        "runtime_envelope": {
          "required_cells": [],
          "cross_host_required_for_pilot": false,
          "status": "unresolved"
        },
        "promotion_rule": "Change-class-specific proof plus all hard gates; no aggregate compensation.",
        "rollback_trigger": "Any protected regression or stale bound evidence.",
        "source_clause_hashes": [
          {
            "sha256": "3ebb7063465ac352008213ff56be4c37dc61268b06eed193c0e1749726d6b47e",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "Create a coherent, visually rigorous deck that communicates one clear narrative, works interactively as a self-contained 16:9 HTML presentation, and can be exported predictably to exact-size PNG images and a visually faithful image-only PPTX when requested."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "93915ae24e39e06d542e7c755cf5ace37ffbd4e607be03be5a576862d5cafa22",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "1. **Interactive HTML only** \u2014 editable source, keyboard navigation, deep links, fullscreen, and presenter notes."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "42cda4870b2bfc628235ba1aed4d5fb42dc53d47c74d3cf792a5624607c16867",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "3. **PPTX** \u2014 a widescreen, image-only PowerPoint assembled from the PNGs."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "bf13c58aea843a6c029b0b283ddf6af96fd16b47da57807f9a02955289c10616",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "Do not ask again when the request already names a format. If the user cannot decide, recommend HTML plus PNG for portability, or all formats when a conventional presentation file is a delivery requirement. Explain that the bundled PPTX workflow preserves appearance exactly but does not make individual slide elements editable."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "03a60842ee4217f0c70a2146c25eca37d12c698da1c52145ad287761ab6ac748",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "\u251c\u2500\u2500 images/                         # only when packaged local assets are used"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "e3fec4a4c31cbfaafa345d9223dc233cd296eeab9e643a3898d61f006026cbd6",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "\u251c\u2500\u2500 ASSET-ATTRIBUTION.md            # only when attribution must travel with the deck"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "63cb250ddacc8d3571d8971405dd1edfa8209e1b6042269c1591b98dff48cb16",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "\u251c\u2500\u2500 slides/                         # only when PNG or PPTX was requested"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "0c380d06cebc20d889603e272c780897ab42af4ec93432810290713930912372",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "\u2514\u2500\u2500 <deck-slug>.pptx                # only when PPTX was requested"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "8335999789d2a1939d39ca5cce33d80fffd6f1812b690d75864038a8bb26a10b",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "Treat the deck directory as one deliverable. Do not place exported `slide-*.png` files in `images/`; `images/` is reserved for deck-ready assets referenced by the HTML. Keep source notes or research beside the deck only when the user asks for them."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "a4e7ffe4bdbb75a2e202833581fd939427d19158e81dc488e3232d15968e0e4c",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "Gather only information that materially changes the deck. Use existing context instead of interrogating the user."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "99ca1fed22d076d1eea57a8e9e25622c717db22cad98eefac88e0325403938ce",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- core narrative and required sections"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "1010dae3e792d635febf21cce7fdf3d0febadae76fba9c84e428bd9adab9382e",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "When evidence is incomplete, label assumptions and illustrative values explicitly. Never invent a source, quotation, customer claim, or measured result."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "871b670700fa282fd9edcc7994612508258a09f2c57468f5f7b267c6914730b0",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "6. **Validate the live DOM at the target viewport.** Check slide state, clipping, collisions, required wording, console errors, and interactive controls before trusting screenshots."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "c0964b31df48e79d2e997459b0cf2b317fcfb4826a6146d45a18a61c0ef8aadf",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "7. **Export only when requested.** Produce PNGs in one browser process, verify every image, then build PPTX from the verified PNGs."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "c368aada7ad2ae3e46dc6e69e326138e18110c416ba355da5efaf2e733ceecd1",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- Prefer a few large elements over many small ones. Do not shrink text to rescue an overloaded slide; simplify the slide."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "cd1dbb9786cb12a73531386f784a530faf34eea6e30829d014babd69224473be",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- Avoid decorative gradients, shadows, or animation that compete with the story. Motion should clarify slide entry or focus and must be disabled for export."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "20d5d8873e0f502daa783cefa41ffee4e3a6b4eaf42c4dcd087f9ba48a74294a",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- Preserve whitespace. Never solve hierarchy by filling every available area."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "6dc00c037abb6927a805f48e5eb4fd2dd54160289eacf7ff204d81fa7bab7bf5",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "The runtime must maintain exactly one active slide during normal viewing. Implement:"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "6678f634b899e3f665d975cdcd8279c3165768dbd8f4af8a6625e83ce480027c",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- visible next/previous controls that do not cover slide content"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "a80b3a9fa3e058122089fb55550c1a468370baecd4636a8d04230fa5d39cb0d8",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "Keep presentation state in a small, readable script. Do not add a framework for a single-file deck."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "60b1cb5e2d981735d8cb77097498eaaa7c9afa286654213ae8e1ea99cae09375",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "Use the following contract whenever a deck contains user-provided or locally generated image files. Do not invent, scrape, or silently download imagery."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "de0a8a6bb6b20f2686289f8f6e535632afd05aeb917c0061fd39a729aa4f7af8",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- **Single-file HTML (default):** keep deck-ready files under `images/` while authoring, then embed their bytes as data URIs in the final `index.html`. The delivered HTML must render correctly without the authoring directory."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "ac640e81a5aed43fcaca67a7262fffc5089b0f565d58f949600c9e0faa9eb367",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- **Portable package:** when the user approves local assets or embedding would make the HTML unreasonable, keep the files under `<deck-slug>/images/` and reference them only with relative paths such as `images/photo-team-workshop.webp`. The whole deck directory is the deliverable."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "3956f4197c97e864c44725d4a269789f382970178177eb6d170b15261bc388ba",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "Never leave absolute paths, `file://` URLs, temporary paths, or unapproved `http://`/`https://` image dependencies in the final HTML."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "51affd6780d818e12070a0430caf7e233add8f22ed664ad3b2e80120073465f7",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- Keep `images/` flat by default and store only deck-ready assets there. Keep untouched originals outside the deliverable."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "b58bf4c0fc935785758d43fbede42383ebbc204307efda2279dcedf4976d6a3c",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- Use SVG for trusted diagrams and logos, WebP or JPEG for photographs, and PNG for screenshots or transparency. The extension must match the encoded format."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "ce0f83d836171725ac100e0eb4159538d83edbc2872b320d09f696102d758de4",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- Preserve source aspect ratio. Create a deck-ready copy for cropping, compression, metadata removal, or color adjustment; do not silently modify the user's original."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "af3329b8fce958829e2a18d5f8bced679674430e30a816701198cda79433d33f",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- Remove unneeded EXIF or GPS metadata before external distribution. Preserve attribution and license details in `<deck-slug>/ASSET-ATTRIBUTION.md` when they must travel with the deck, without copying private source URLs or credentials. Keep `images/` reserved for actual deck-ready image files."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "bec3da315cb7f5b1f8b59c524b8fe62d14501cf7325f0392c98a30e037ef391f",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- Treat SVG as active content: inline only trusted, sanitized SVG without scripts, event handlers, `foreignObject`, or external references. Otherwise load it through `<img>`."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "638a27cc8c0caf36dd6a673e9cb171d8f087c91ada3e16e9a97006c66da89a3e",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "Use `<img>` for meaningful imagery so alternative text and load failures remain inspectable. Use CSS backgrounds only for decorative texture, and mark decorative `<img>` elements with `alt=\"\"`."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "aaf8aa3f8e8f2992af1fc5bd7eef03ea1af6130ce09281111156a91ed81e638e",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "Use `cover` for photographs intended to fill a frame. Use `contain` for screenshots, diagrams, charts, and logos that must remain fully visible. Adjust `--image-position` to preserve the focal point; never stretch an image to fit. Set slide images to `loading=\"eager\"`; lazy loading is incompatible with deterministic export because inactive slides may never enter the viewport before validation."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "5c6b5bd638dce792c7cdf3eb46251d63566f56686bc72cea89dfab2a76bd5f1a",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "The bundled PNG exporter performs this broken-image check after page load and aborts before taking screenshots. Do not treat a placeholder, missing image icon, or CSS background as a successful export."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "85b9f3dd4cbec40077385774615a95edf3d58babf2da7b884d6fd530f8d1ee35",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "Every deck intended for export must support an explicit `?export=1` mode and an equivalent `body.export` class. Export mode must hide interface chrome and remove nondeterministic motion while leaving slide content untouched."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "47afac7939add6cf46ad4ccfbf8251e319594d57cf131af8610c03e51e116687",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "The interactive URL without `?export=1` must restore controls, progress, and notes behavior. Test both modes; an export stylesheet that permanently hides controls is a defect."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "c6337ba7030e35b036f825f65e2c014697bf5140cbce366d75b8ce96c3300cb1",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "Store notes with each slide in a hidden `.speaker-note` element so notes travel with the standalone file. Render the active slide's notes into a separate notes panel only when the presenter toggles it."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "5f1aa592ab4b243aedf6a6034850d031a0669fa50311256a7ffd1080e2810de6",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- do not expose hidden notes in PNG export"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "896526a64d3d3da2b89625a91eb0cc91c6a6321306af2caa2d7fb0458a6aa9d4",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "Validate the actual page, not only the source text."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "37450c02e1136b76572c6dc689487529cb00307323b3f650e8718c35b15d1098",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- controls are visible interactively and hidden only in export mode"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "29bfc265e29209ed73d0c63efb5a6f4b80f122b420be8662ba54d184b597ab82",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "Also check the browser console, required phrases, dates, units, business-context labels, citations, and caveats. A clean accessibility tree and correct DOM state are stronger evidence than a single screenshot."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "d34aec33cff8d27fa62bd36063ba2f40b14166c63d9de2ba08f95768df189cd0",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "Use `--force` only when replacing existing `slide-*.png` files is intended. The exporter defaults to `.slide`, discovers the count in page JavaScript, adds `body.export`, waits briefly for native paint using the configurable settle delay, and fails on timeout or missing output."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "434df11453d4f8f75627cf672eb64b711b244bbf7848b1f543d99886c4e0f27c",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "Use native OCR or image inspection for representative content when available, but do not treat OCR as a substitute for DOM geometry checks."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "f7a46ee34751a3cdbe403cd651ac5e7cce0dccf4f76910bf911bf6c8eb19e835",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "If Playwright or Puppeteer is already part of the environment, use one browser process and one page, set the viewport once, activate slides sequentially, and capture each slide. Do not add a browser dependency merely for convenience without telling the user. Do not spawn one Chrome process per slide; that pattern is slow, can leave orphan processes, and becomes worse when parallelized."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "b21570e3b3d996f48c4aa55918cd86bb36afd81f26d86ccd231b478946308847",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "Do not promise editable PPTX conversion unless a separate native-slide authoring workflow is explicitly requested and validated."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "358bf182fbd13ae62df1f773e88120182111bcaf16cb06f6afc284b181fb565e",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "Only upload when the user explicitly requests Google Slides and the local `gws` CLI is authenticated. Convert the PPTX through Drive, dry-run first, then verify the presentation:"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "bd6bfe40e8a6a4339c34c4a6af4318f56c3c6898fae5a2b77655ec8a319afe36",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "Run the same command without `--dry-run` only after reviewing the request. Verify with `gws slides presentations get` that page size is widescreen, slide count matches, and each image-only slide has exactly one image."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "276b94ecb5b12b6fa52c9df7d4f71f490388d3547bfd7d14bf0595b1ecb665bb",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- **Stale DevTools screenshots:** a browser screenshot tool may return a stale compositor frame even when the DOM and accessibility tree show the correct active slide. Retry through a deterministic exporter and verify the output file; do not accept the stale capture as proof."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "94f639b63e0b66f36a306bb792a6790cf7ca8e9f679ddb6523abd0154a158f8e",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- **Single-pass print-to-PDF timeouts:** do not make PDF printing the default route to PNG. Snapshot slides individually in one loaded page."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "8bec49733b3ab2060f9549c144311f9a9e7e754d3b02428ea28feabd350f1cf6",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- **Invalid bitmap configuration:** four samples per pixel with `hasAlpha: false` is inconsistent. The macOS exporter must use RGBA: `samplesPerPixel: 4` and `hasAlpha: true`."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "391bc820d1e3228249c6bd040c99bf8339ec9d772f5487b5c04782b5932f9b65",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- **Hidden interactive controls:** export-mode rules must be scoped under `body.export`, not applied globally."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "9409a5c623989119a6cb02f83a15f74a92aaed729f6580bc75422bc9c0752beb",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- **Overflow rescued by tiny text:** do not reduce readability to pass bounds checks; split or simplify the slide."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "c6bdabd7a499f8083ba614f5c559dc67e374acfd43b90208925384780305131a",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- **Unlabeled sample data:** mark illustrative metrics and replace them before final delivery when factual evidence is required."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "e7909c49d951ff2a0cc19bc8bddb8f25974829e8f568a8243d11ea351f41d0f8",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- forbidden: transmit private source material to third parties without authorization, invent evidence, silently scrape external assets, or claim export success without checking generated files"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "10c0567eea1c46d9a0ec517171a1f6a49cdf0164964a282c77ebded65ef7a43e",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- Disable animation and hide controls only in explicit export mode."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "a01802c116ea35e204467f0c5e94206aecea620109f5185e15d5a99a35d552a8",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- Create PPTX only from verified PNGs."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "f5cb7f400590aeb3488f2b8d2b6e5bedccbe6395189bcae1740c97e2b8610008",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- Label flattened PPTX output as image-only and non-editable."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "01f6f2692376cbeaaf463c85658399cdbcfd80c47af06f8837d3373943d95738",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- Use `images/` only for deck-ready referenced image files, with descriptive kebab-case names and relative paths; keep attribution metadata at deck root."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "30a27b16beacdd707b84358ac53ec279615400652d6319123c31c0c1b3248655",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- Never silently fetch imagery or distort an image to fit a frame."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "77357dbdaba34183181a2940a8cdce735aae457d5f4694b620c0fe81799c73b6",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "## Required Inputs"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "3d4b9f171064970a2e9947e6e3f0fb13501d9ced9a9ac9ebe2cde123882829ec",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "## Required Output"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "37c5572c2d9b73d7805bf7f7268862b16a8e249353af55f152449c34fbbee3ad",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "Every substantial writer-authored delivery artifact must include:"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "63aba0b7aa9bc2b18012fe9fe48da0ef47292afe956c8b2ee0b10504e845e293",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- `Export Tradeoffs` \u2014 platform requirements and image-only PPTX limitation"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "e0e6ce5d81e0ded4f04b0e7361742d9c92907d243f269282ebb32cd67a57f48e",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "### Example Request: HTML Only"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "35936dce0414067103c3a029ea219c4e7a8ba33c270256c63c07a1f6ae761353",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "> Turn this technical proposal into a polished browser presentation. Keep it self-contained and do not create images or upload anything."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "f89b4bc05206bc8c887f13656e1091599326c5e7a542fcbc864e5c4bd42f0cfc",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- [ ] Required attribution travels at deck root without private source URLs or credentials."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "4a5790c20da905195f92e60711f9de21f20cfcc55fc1a46bfa2a6ae084840dd3",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "| Export safety | Export mode is explicit, motionless, and hides only presentation chrome |"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "fac7308fc753e7364810b482102da1e7e819381425febf8aedd509d7ef140b6b",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "Existing domain checks, source rules, uncertainty labels, required artifact contents and permission boundaries remain mandatory. Producing an artifact includes its domain observations or findings; the independent review findings below are a separate list of defects in that artifact. Required output formats apply to the writer's artifact, not coordinator dispatches or reviewer findings. Completing an author checklist or assigning an author score does not accept the artifact. This review does not replace another workflow's approval, identity, path-fit or bounded return protocol, and grants no wider execution authority."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "283e7be539f472b9be3611179d19aa6dcb47a7d6be2764415c7e007a45e1dd1d",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- **Writer**: writes the artifact only and repairs it from the review findings. Resume the same writer for every revision; do not start a fresh writer for a revision."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "dea1be25a70cb9c3b76aec16b97d9fbc43e09d315850ca53a095b5979399cdeb",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "- **Reviewer**: did not write the artifact, checks claims against the sources and retained domain rules, and writes findings only. The reviewer does not rewrite the artifact. Resume the same reviewer for every later round."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "32659bf6e33c011c3144f25db8d302cc6162072c987fd8cf23e4b4a1c5b5a84c",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "Use actual separate participants. If they or their resumed contexts are unavailable, report required review as incomplete; do not substitute self-review, coordinator authorship or simulated roles. Each participant stays within the existing allowed reads, writes and checks."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "420f35be46a1e2897db9a15706174ebb232e5c4ec39ec538a64eeab0e9adfe80",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "2. The coordinator dispatches the current artifact, original task and sources to the separate reviewer. The reviewer is hostile in the ordinary sense: verify each material claim, cite the source, and do not invent a defect to fill a section. Unsupported claims, misleading certainty or omitted required uncertainty warrant source-grounded findings; a clearly labeled permitted gap is not itself proof of a defect."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "ddb7354cd7f77d788c2dbbbe162d7d65f9699f0123127b140402db5149370349",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "4. The coordinator returns every open finding to the same writer. The writer repairs the artifact and responds to each received identifier with `addressed` and what changed, `wontfix` and a technical reason, or `needs-user-input` when only a human can choose. These are repair dispositions, not authored review findings or acceptance decisions. Findings awaiting a human answer remain unresolved."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "ee18a182fff070e270d8848d35b7ce527647fed86ac15c70c9814cdb3ca9e93d",
            "source": "ssot/engos-content-dynamic-html-presentations.md",
            "text": "6. The coordinator counts the reviewer's current open findings and resumes the same writer and reviewer until the reviewer explicitly reports zero open findings on the current artifact. There is no round cap. Do not finalize while any finding is open, while a required human answer is pending or while required review is incomplete. The inner finding count does not decide acceptance by a wider workflow."
          }
        ],
        "review_status": "draft"
      },
