          },
          {
            "id": "engos-design-architecture:L581:56dd7611e73f",
            "heading": "Pattern Red Flags / Reject These Moves",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-architecture.md",
            "source_line": 591,
            "sha256": "56dd7611e73fa179a0b67675769339a4c602880433be8fbd4339fc549298c064",
            "text": "- pattern recommendations that do not improve testability, replaceability, or ownership",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-design-architecture:L597:3417c6dd3d4d",
            "heading": "Required System Outputs",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-architecture.md",
            "source_line": 607,
            "sha256": "3417c6dd3d4d592ad7f2d15a7fe70eefb29cb9074c82b2875816482e6537a7d9",
            "text": "#### Required System Outputs",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-design-architecture:L805:c7a2a9e98efd",
            "heading": "Hard Constraints",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-architecture.md",
            "source_line": 815,
            "sha256": "c7a2a9e98efd0bf74869f7c5a7c547c7ddbe083d813720ecb4b4a3202c787a50",
            "text": "1. Never return an architecture recommendation without stating objective, scope, assumptions, and constraints.",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-design-architecture:L806:02e40b3d1442",
            "heading": "Hard Constraints",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-architecture.md",
            "source_line": 816,
            "sha256": "02e40b3d1442595bd1248ccc3778f403e566faf362024f1d2dabab681e415709",
            "text": "2. Never recommend a major design without at least one rejected alternative.",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-design-architecture:L807:365f9818c152",
            "heading": "Hard Constraints",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-architecture.md",
            "source_line": 817,
            "sha256": "365f9818c152b00d703a65cba71a754209d74c8fea94a912abb4d8859c4f09cc",
            "text": "3. Never recommend a schema, interface, or topology change without migration and rollback guidance.",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-design-architecture:L808:c22bdb1b8e81",
            "heading": "Hard Constraints",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-architecture.md",
            "source_line": 818,
            "sha256": "c22bdb1b8e81e64035cd0cb2ae6f8bc02bcb07c9445af767638e98202d56eb90",
            "text": "4. Never hide uncertainty. Mark unknowns explicitly.",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-design-architecture:L809:5f14ddd9ba49",
            "heading": "Hard Constraints",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-architecture.md",
            "source_line": 819,
            "sha256": "5f14ddd9ba49c2d925eb639b65add54ddf731260764fe3148f26dd12840cae13",
            "text": "5. Never confuse module boundaries with deployment boundaries.",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-design-architecture:L810:44bc24df870f",
            "heading": "Hard Constraints",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-architecture.md",
            "source_line": 820,
            "sha256": "44bc24df870fbcf16f8a710bdd584336afce4b865a2b66b2228b71dfbcc04a53",
            "text": "6. Never couple the recommendation to one vendor or framework unless the constraint is explicit.",
            "kind": "guarded_invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-design-architecture:L811:822a5d36365e",
            "heading": "Hard Constraints",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-architecture.md",
            "source_line": 821,
            "sha256": "822a5d36365e7910204b4640ae4b39cf825644b9ea245c2cd8e45eff9c614223",
            "text": "7. Never claim an architecture is scalable, reliable, or secure without naming the mechanism that makes it so.",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-design-architecture:L812:46836c815a5e",
            "heading": "Hard Constraints",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-architecture.md",
            "source_line": 822,
            "sha256": "46836c815a5ecec4e49e2981742bb7cc8247592e8e2f26b18160025c89c9df84",
            "text": "8. Never produce pseudo-authoritative numbers without showing assumptions.",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-design-architecture:L813:c05c6928302d",
            "heading": "Hard Constraints",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-architecture.md",
            "source_line": 823,
            "sha256": "c05c6928302db122864f383fc826be21b816c2d92b87615a89a3aaaca92dcbf9",
            "text": "9. Never optimize for novelty over maintainability.",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-design-architecture:L814:e9c762ef592f",
            "heading": "Hard Constraints",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-architecture.md",
            "source_line": 824,
            "sha256": "e9c762ef592f96f46ab4acca0d1204e5499ccd0498508bf879f7f053c64a3fb0",
            "text": "10. Never omit validation steps for a meaningful change.",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-design-architecture:L815:37eab6d753da",
            "heading": "Hard Constraints",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-architecture.md",
            "source_line": 825,
            "sha256": "37eab6d753da10803ff5466fd12973ad267daa0f8ea47d09fc0ec32850fc87ec",
            "text": "11. Never claim a component is removable, isolated, or decoupled without naming a falsifier and stating whether the check is proposed or observed.",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-design-architecture:L816:31def904306a",
            "heading": "Hard Constraints",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-architecture.md",
            "source_line": 826,
            "sha256": "31def904306a60116d15d7d0b9945803f4970bf44d60ab782fb0f621adb7e0fb",
            "text": "12. Never present a convention as an enforced boundary; identify its contract or check.",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-design-architecture:L817:819a3b3c1df5",
            "heading": "Hard Constraints",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-architecture.md",
            "source_line": 827,
            "sha256": "819a3b3c1df533483a07094dbf597dee2658654e19c4178d3494a6cc6ab8c146",
            "text": "13. Never silently recommend raising an existing ratchet baseline; state the avoidable-versus-intrinsic design judgment.",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-design-architecture:L818:e1734b6c6f19",
            "heading": "Hard Constraints",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-architecture.md",
            "source_line": 828,
            "sha256": "e1734b6c6f198831520795df6228039639e107630c563ce1822b4a4c3c38b1a7",
            "text": "14. Never turn an architecture recommendation into a code-health metric scan or drift report; use supplied measurements with attribution.",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-design-architecture:L823:6fd80bda8e52",
            "heading": "Recommendation Roles",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-architecture.md",
            "source_line": 833,
            "sha256": "6fd80bda8e52ba5a50f5ca2336eb66c116bd167765a026c01ad7d00f9f8cbbea",
            "text": "- **Writer**: writes the recommendation artifact only and repairs it from the reviewer's findings. Resume the same writer for every revision; do not start a fresh writer for a revision.",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-design-architecture:L824:9eca3af8a0ce",
            "heading": "Recommendation Roles",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-architecture.md",
            "source_line": 834,
            "sha256": "9eca3af8a0ce19f969affc68eb1a7da3e060cbb3ec64716249d8c6a77538cafc",
            "text": "- **Reviewer**: did not write the artifact, checks it against the sources and retained domain rules, and writes findings only. The reviewer does not rewrite the artifact. Resume the same reviewer for every later round.",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-design-architecture:L826:3903553b1d77",
            "heading": "Recommendation Roles",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-architecture.md",
            "source_line": 836,
            "sha256": "3903553b1d77c60f4c464d709b0f98d8583c9a3e2a53c7031628f81d64fb2b47",
            "text": "If separate participants or their resumed contexts are unavailable, report the review as incomplete. Never substitute coordinator authorship, self-review, or simulated roles for a required participant.",
            "kind": "guarded_invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-design-architecture:L830:56e72662b3ee",
            "heading": "Review Gate",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-architecture.md",
            "source_line": 840,
            "sha256": "56e72662b3ee1c9164a04352d5413eedfaebd76d4b4ac6c8f9ce51e7d7b3aad8",
            "text": "2. The coordinator gives the separate reviewer the artifact, original task, sources and domain rules. The reviewer is hostile in the ordinary sense: verify each material claim, cite the source, and do not invent a defect to fill a section. A source gap is grounds for a finding only when the artifact overstates evidence, misses a required uncertainty, or cannot support a material decision.",
            "kind": "guarded_invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-design-architecture:L832:d1b53933b583",
            "heading": "Review Gate",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-architecture.md",
            "source_line": 842,
            "sha256": "d1b53933b583b89fffb5c0925a70fded51248142dda5afa058b036619efa0e69",
            "text": "4. The coordinator returns every open finding to the same writer. The writer repairs the artifact and attaches a disposition to each received identifier: `addressed` with what changed; `wontfix` with a technical reason; or `needs-user-input` when only a human can choose. These dispositions are repair responses, not a replacement finding list or acceptance decision. Human-choice findings remain unresolved while awaiting the answer.",
            "kind": "guarded_invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-design-architecture:L834:de06f47fc160",
            "heading": "Review Gate",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-architecture.md",
            "source_line": 844,
            "sha256": "de06f47fc160cc836c5f040092a1cb9434b29b7a10233c6e9a3e98113aafe0c8",
            "text": "6. The coordinator counts the reviewer's current open findings and resumes the same writer and reviewer until the reviewer explicitly reports zero open findings on the current artifact. There is no round cap. Do not finalize while findings are open, while a required human answer is pending, or while review is incomplete. A writer's score or checklist cannot satisfy this exit. This inner issue count does not decide any wider workflow's acceptance.",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
