        "source_clause_hashes": [
          {
            "sha256": "eacfed697b7275e5a35daaf972196c112bc33be319f62870f9e8788bcc67d01e",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "Compile a reviewed plan or implementation intent into a host-aware goal packet that a long-running coding agent can execute without treating chat memory as the source of truth. Use this skill after or during read-only planning when the user wants a durable goal, specification, and verifier. Do not use it for a simple one-step task, an ordinary implementation request that does not need a goal loop, or a request to run an unsupported native Goal command."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "d198bfb7ae3137354bca459e11fe2cebd3fab1e5c40c7edcee59a9a9a9da4f76",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- select only versioned, verified host adapters and report unsupported native runners explicitly"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "253f6cf16c615c62c001e4bcc33d90279cff53422b1909b857c80fbce580d7e1",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- implementing the compiled goal or changing product source while the skill is in read-only planning mode"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "fd413473c9bab432561333ff95c44a3ec791721a5d4bf1015ce1961b2343468b",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- manufacturing a long-running goal for a completed, one-step, watch-only, or otherwise unsuitable task"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "ed38acb60cd7f4acbf8e5ce8195c2f4c82b374e6d0ec04af2d7fa496e4d70aac",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "Load `resources/adapters/hosts.json` and select the adapter matching the active product and measured version. Recheck the installed version when possible. Do not generalize one host's command grammar, size limit, iteration mechanism, file behavior, or Plan-mode permissions to another host."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "d139c04ddda258b3a725d70740271956aed7e1ab107157c69b70e97aa2b87940",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- Codex has native Goal mode or goal tools and a 4,000-character persisted objective. Do not invent an iteration flag or translate iterations into a token budget."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "f9cf7abfc6e7beacd11b6246bc1f698c0f8707b034362877d668d149f4153179",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- A custom runner is supported only after its adapter records versioned evidence for grammar, persistence, size, budget, and stopping behavior."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "5f628fce0da6ccb4bdf6a2ad536ec67e54404b2cdb72f7e6a21545ef9f0a79f1",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "Write `goal.txt` as wrapper-free prose. Count only its contents, not `/goal`, flags, quoting, or launcher syntax."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "b4d322f30989c5868c4dab89e28db2e3e2a0dd41ca3dbb62fed2f401de5c1a43",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "These preferred values are heuristics, not behavioral proof. Move overflow into `spec.md`; never raise the cap to preserve detail."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "c9b610c83a09c740a76659dfb7dacac74871dcd0f8480cf6b9e02ab4adacc6ae",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "7. `STOP / REPORT` \u2014 stale, blocked, approval-required, no-progress, exhausted, and achieved behavior plus receipt path"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "0be6fc7bce33c795e2baeca9c59cb2e16d94d35e3b5c384cd383e9bf31ae8e28",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "Do not place evidence dumps, long file inventories, source commentary, design rationale, or full task lists in `goal.txt`."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "af933f4e8b0933e9dc8cb531ca2eedf2af23c650629c74fb89f92d95a830bd14",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "10. Ask only for decisions that cannot be discovered and would materially change scope, safety, or acceptance."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "8c45fa7059eb9c185de3c36c431576e2efc5ec9d264dabba9f337e1fe84c8848",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "Put the receipt in `spec.md`. The executor must repeat a lightweight current-state and rule preflight before editing. Material drift yields `STALE_PACKET`; the executor must not silently rewrite the goal or verifier."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "eba3ee6da9d0734d451e52d5ff6962b5d9de2b8ede1abcf2f4221523c2cc4de3",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "`spec.md` must contain:"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "60c4b0b8b283ae3fee8dcb6c91adac9fcb506c8abfcddd1b309569f2048df953",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- behavioral requirements and acceptance criteria; use EARS only where it improves testability"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "8180750feadbc112b64fa9433857c518d291dac5d1145a67eb91205e523afb64",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "Prefer one goal. Split into ordered packets only when outcomes have different independent value, verifiers, owners, or approval boundaries, or when no single verifier can judge the complete result."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "7cf117d5879268ba14d41c46cd4ce3304ad0157d059ca57c022d08118391306b",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- `self_check`: controlled by the executor; never sufficient for completion"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "1987ab66fd8728630e84d457d47fb9db0f4c7542c69c34ef434b1404b97a6327",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "Hashes prove tamper evidence, not independence. The verifier must:"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "d6a2c2a636cd66fb3e5254ccc7317d29329e6281b30ac21c50b919db60ae2c33",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- evaluate only the named criterion when `CRITERION_ID=<id>` is set, emitting the exact line `CRITERION <id> PASS` with exit `0` when its condition is present or `CRITERION <id> FAIL` with exit `1` when absent; invalid or unverifiable input uses a distinct error and must not fall through to the full suite"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "39132c35920cd442442cc99dffda44a87c859f6b6ae7925429c02dc9c3b5d8a2",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- pass every entry in `criterion-flips.json`: the exact criterion logic must be executed against synthetic condition-present and condition-absent trees and its verdict must flip in the required direction"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "78285bd988278cbf2f9af2574706d60a0fb2ae0e7791fcfed669c5f088c27c5d",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- fail if required tests or behaviors are missing, not only when existing tests fail"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "37e9e3f6396740886c6d1d1f866557dc7302e892c7981b91ac5c56f562de81f3",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- disclose operator-only and unobservable criteria"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "984d4cd5fc1ad651d05fef2c2086e617bb0897c8df9600c4d4a68811637c8f46",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "If the verifier passes either the untouched tree or cheapest fake, refuse `SEALED_READY`. Require an independent audit before returning `NO_GOAL_NEEDED`; a permissive verifier is not proof that the goal already exists. Run verifiers with `bash verify.sh`; never require their execute bit."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "17adf32600f187be3d0b9e9e144f0f6a69c785b6091d076961bb010364da6902",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "1. use a durable goal/spec location required by repository policy"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "7fda01cdc91061423e92930c8bc79dc3b14e80732d12bbd018c0bd3278219f20",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "3. for cloud or remote execution, use a repo-accessible committed or uploaded packet only with approval"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "0d20c48ce631b70d70b6b7b35cb16fd3c978d7a15eec9a1310ea71293368cee8",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "Plan mode may be read-only. Draft inline as `DRAFTED_UNSEALED`; do not claim that files exist. After approval or a permitted mode transition, materialize the exact draft and run the bundled packet helper."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "f4337ebd5d68275ff7708e19666a279b6e89397fd83f769b794a758e2311e981",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "2. Decide whether a long-running goal is warranted. Return `NO_GOAL_NEEDED` for a truly complete or one-step outcome only after evidence supports that decision."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "c6b2ceb08935441696e6580f37ff1f6a0470598edb163622690c481bcb77dea5",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "5. In read-only Plan mode, return the exact draft as `DRAFTED_UNSEALED` and name the required materialization action."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "261cfb95ef141d45ee01619c3f0bd2f64412f7687dea1e699bc88942e9f645b0",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "7. Run `bash resources/goal-lint --tree <untouched-tree> --hostile-tree <cheapest-fake-tree> <packet-dir>`. Fix every finding; warnings must be acknowledged in the spec."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "a35d66913d9b556e9001c584b4b7396b79a742e037422ac5b2026e2543073aae",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "9. Run `python3 resources/scripts/goal_packet.py seal <packet-dir>`. Seal only when size, schema, paths, repository binding, artifact hashes, adapter support, falsifiability, and hostile-pass checks succeed."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "76c288a2a021e620f216b60d3bee25836a9f6c8dfdb7bdc7bff3608cc66a92d0",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "11. Emit the wrapper-free goal, host-native budget, and launch command only when the adapter supports one."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "b20ebd5feae6575149f4952da894c220d50d9c4076597ccafae8b817e004e135",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "12. Honor a user-supplied budget. Otherwise use a verified host default when one exists. Never invent Claude/Gemini iteration flags or convert iteration counts into Codex token budgets."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "517914351fa304a38d29c1d4d77e6f4c9a12d75b6b4c9eb6530442a56f28e036",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- Preserve the user's literal outcome; do not redefine success around an easier subset."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "72976d60b178aa78e76a8bb40c4f1a89cbf68f26cf6c6c1c7f4b57e30be9f2ed",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- Do not write packet paths while the active mode forbids writes."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "9919e84c6c0033485471e882b8baf0106ce38ee6796254a94e62190c65b17a6a",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- Do not call a writable verifier independent."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "f801c581c85d9f2666cebed31b909a514d3a0e075b011cf7aebf007a35baa31d",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- Do not design the anchor after the implementation plan or park a load-bearing outcome check in advisory output."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "da71f2de36ef81fd4b7dbf625488f9abd108d1eafdfdb1d90961085a8fbb1180",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- Do not make bulk population execution the goal anchor; prove the mechanism over a bounded sample and route bulk work to its authorization-owning policy or routine."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "02116aca08c6b600c53552213cc904b2e71f7ac9fa42cd19a4884cf7da3e3998",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- Do not freeze an identifier that appears in any exclusion or do-not-touch list."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "8e7583343a6a115ce384dcd8e0375fbacd0db426912c83ef5a754bf1ad03c29e",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- Do not accept a criterion that returns the same verdict for condition-present and condition-absent trees, returns an error instead of a valid verdict, or is absent from the verifier inventory."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "261f81ed1bb69e57e1578738c864ecd66ec6bcbaf40180bf69a495e21ca3ea9a",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- Do not trust a repaired judge until its amendment discloses the diff, old/new hashes, and criterion impact."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "6e4a02c19d03718ef64e8a8a04ebac825e083ca2eee56e2a51e7efd91cb72ef3",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- Do not seal while any of the five manual design answers is blank."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "c244b7cf14a664f75d451a03044c58f3cf8d2115edf6fa4f7820a8225fb9947f",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- Do not emit a launch command for an unsupported or unverified runner."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "a71324d791b62368ac534bd8bb61c9c472ce1a1dcd6d8b13df3765b9fabae1b4",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- Do not call `structural_ready`, a sealed packet, green local tests, or a model review behavioral promotion."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "77357dbdaba34183181a2940a8cdce735aae457d5f4694b620c0fe81799c73b6",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "## Required Inputs"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "3d4b9f171064970a2e9947e6e3f0fb13501d9ced9a9ac9ebe2cde123882829ec",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "## Required Output"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "932aa7c83ac52c39170c8d64df46d56613284b1eff958f7dfac06b333ad0839e",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "For `DRAFTED_UNSEALED`, `Launch Command` must be `null`. For `UNSUPPORTED_NATIVE_GOAL`, keep the packet useful but state which runner contract is missing. For `SEALED_READY`, report goal characters, UTF-8 bytes, adapter version, repository binding, artifact hashes, baseline verifier result, and exact command."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "4f10bcd36e3a3bc2c357b543f6f34d885a0506fdffe15fd706f6b4973a919b3b",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- Do not mutate source code while compiling a packet in read-only Plan mode."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "fa5888cf9993572e26d60adc691a1e48f1f3d10a008dff6a9bcb093daea3578b",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- Do not use chat history as the only durable source for a long-running goal."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "7828eed5e9d99986d5b87a446e125d12b96124ff6858071073b9e4c304827ff1",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- Do not exceed 3,500 characters or bytes even when a host permits more."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "6a43727b9ff85bf8ac279f16f55beff80da695c1f5763b21b657da37c4c32a92",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- Do not hide unknowns, unsupported behavior, manual checks, or external-state dependencies."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "e888923a8526ecbaf0e8a02c53d8a35957d3b30e2162e4bde6a43dca5e97588e",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- Do not rely on an execute bit for bundled scripts or task verifiers; invoke Bash and Python resources through their interpreters."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "2e03ca91acae146a6cbef1e1c035ea4da8d8cbb24305cb21fd45610dc1659285",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- Do not create, replace, pause, resume, or clear a goal unless the user separately requests that runtime action."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "1bc598d434913342be15be8131d93e349a77aa51ea641074f0cb33cb3b8b643c",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- Do not deploy, commit, merge, or alter global skill installations merely because the packet is ready."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "e307de3c6676e0bd7343354904990d2e49ed803ad44ad0460003c1a773abd09b",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "Compile the packet, then return `UNSUPPORTED_NATIVE_GOAL` unless a tested custom Gemini runner adapter is installed. Do not invent a command from Kiro syntax."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "133a07647c3b24f6f4b189ec1102407c03a7b8d8ec590b8f692e1d682316b34d",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "| Host accuracy | Only verified commands, limits, and budget mechanisms are emitted |"
          },
          {
            "sha256": "c5ffccd5ec48fc28ba01d2e7efc13ad70ce1e8a1fbdd98bbcf469793b58b50e9",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "Apply this review to a substantial authored goal, specification and verifier packet, whether drafted inline or materialized with authorization. Keep all existing research, verifier-trust, synthetic-tree, lint, seal, drift and launch checks; independent semantic review is an additional artifact prerequisite, not a substitute for those checks. Review the current packet before returning it as ready, and re-run affected deterministic checks after writer repairs. Existing independent audit of a no-goal-needed claim remains required. The inner uncapped review does not alter the compiled task execution budget, stop conditions, runner support or operator approvals."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "fac7308fc753e7364810b482102da1e7e819381425febf8aedd509d7ef140b6b",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "Existing domain checks, source rules, uncertainty labels, required artifact contents and permission boundaries remain mandatory. Producing an artifact includes its domain observations or findings; the independent review findings below are a separate list of defects in that artifact. Required output formats apply to the writer's artifact, not coordinator dispatches or reviewer findings. Completing an author checklist or assigning an author score does not accept the artifact. This review does not replace another workflow's approval, identity, path-fit or bounded return protocol, and grants no wider execution authority."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "283e7be539f472b9be3611179d19aa6dcb47a7d6be2764415c7e007a45e1dd1d",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- **Writer**: writes the artifact only and repairs it from the review findings. Resume the same writer for every revision; do not start a fresh writer for a revision."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "dea1be25a70cb9c3b76aec16b97d9fbc43e09d315850ca53a095b5979399cdeb",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "- **Reviewer**: did not write the artifact, checks claims against the sources and retained domain rules, and writes findings only. The reviewer does not rewrite the artifact. Resume the same reviewer for every later round."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "32659bf6e33c011c3144f25db8d302cc6162072c987fd8cf23e4b4a1c5b5a84c",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "Use actual separate participants. If they or their resumed contexts are unavailable, report required review as incomplete; do not substitute self-review, coordinator authorship or simulated roles. Each participant stays within the existing allowed reads, writes and checks."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "420f35be46a1e2897db9a15706174ebb232e5c4ec39ec538a64eeab0e9adfe80",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "2. The coordinator dispatches the current artifact, original task and sources to the separate reviewer. The reviewer is hostile in the ordinary sense: verify each material claim, cite the source, and do not invent a defect to fill a section. Unsupported claims, misleading certainty or omitted required uncertainty warrant source-grounded findings; a clearly labeled permitted gap is not itself proof of a defect."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "ddb7354cd7f77d788c2dbbbe162d7d65f9699f0123127b140402db5149370349",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "4. The coordinator returns every open finding to the same writer. The writer repairs the artifact and responds to each received identifier with `addressed` and what changed, `wontfix` and a technical reason, or `needs-user-input` when only a human can choose. These are repair dispositions, not authored review findings or acceptance decisions. Findings awaiting a human answer remain unresolved."
          },
          {
            "sha256": "ee18a182fff070e270d8848d35b7ce527647fed86ac15c70c9814cdb3ca9e93d",
            "source": "ssot/engos-design-plan-to-goal.md",
            "text": "6. The coordinator counts the reviewer's current open findings and resumes the same writer and reviewer until the reviewer explicitly reports zero open findings on the current artifact. There is no round cap. Do not finalize while any finding is open, while a required human answer is pending or while required review is incomplete. The inner finding count does not decide acceptance by a wider workflow."
          }
        ],
        "review_status": "draft"
      },
