          {
            "id": "engos-meta-supercharge:L168:acb40e65d113",
            "heading": "Turn-Taking Protocol (<=3 Questions)",
            "source": "ssot/engos-meta-supercharge.md",
            "source_line": 177,
            "sha256": "acb40e65d1130f718356e57c91b7cdd5bcf7dd0cde152797b428fbd6b926af95",
            "text": "Never pretend to be the user or answer for them.",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-meta-supercharge:L183:fb53dd951133",
            "heading": "Auto-Routing (Smart Defaults)",
            "source": "ssot/engos-meta-supercharge.md",
            "source_line": 192,
            "sha256": "fb53dd951133fba280145290c1b7985b0a1933a53cbefbdefe466adaac9dd11c",
            "text": "If the user provides no explicit module, SuperCharge MUST route the request to a sensible sequence and announce it:",
            "kind": "guarded_invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-meta-supercharge:L201:832fa678350d",
            "heading": "Reflective Controls (Optional Modifiers)",
            "source": "ssot/engos-meta-supercharge.md",
            "source_line": 210,
            "sha256": "832fa678350d1dfbe163d15f2ae27c89f08d1d119a5a4400410df238193f98e8",
            "text": "If the user supplies more than one reflective control, stop and ask them to choose one; do not silently select, merge, or discard controls. Auto-routing must not add `/safe` when the user supplied another reflective control. Safety constraints still apply regardless of modifier choice.",
            "kind": "guarded_invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-meta-supercharge:L204:cf9a08cacbfd",
            "heading": "Independent Subagents (Core Principle, Not a Module)",
            "source": "ssot/engos-meta-supercharge.md",
            "source_line": 213,
            "sha256": "cf9a08cacbfdfe05220a4090072404d660f534d90298a402c649cd527c890558",
            "text": "Actual independent subagents are mandatory for substantive improvement, review, grading, and verification. Self-review and simulated agent roles are not acceptable substitutes. Recover failed delegation or report required review as incomplete; never claim it passed. Help, example listing, and mode exit are exempt.",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-meta-supercharge:L206:3dde2d8c29af",
            "heading": "Independent Subagents (Core Principle, Not a Module)",
            "source": "ssot/engos-meta-supercharge.md",
            "source_line": 215,
            "sha256": "3dde2d8c29aff165982054544e0ef311b03e95b39daf8209bbdf94b160afab9d",
            "text": "Initial reviewers receive the task, criteria, evidence, full required module resources, and artifact without the author's self-grade or preferred verdict. Preserve necessary factual context. Exchange findings afterward for debate and synthesis. The author cannot approve its own work. Detailed coordination rules are in `resources/references/shared-review.md` and are a dependency of operational routes.",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-meta-supercharge:L211:135a5be3cdc7",
            "heading": "Resource Delivery Gate",
            "source": "ssot/engos-meta-supercharge.md",
            "source_line": 220,
            "sha256": "135a5be3cdc7446bc11536bc4d2a162de614736bef72a90cad9d35edf2267250",
            "text": "For skill surfaces, resolve paths relative to the skill directory. For agent surfaces, resource-map paths resolve relative to the directory containing the bundled `capability.json`. The map uses paths without the `resources/` prefix. Use `python3 \"<resource-root>/scripts/load_module.py\" --route /ult --format text` with the selected exact route (repeat for stacked routes) when the bundled helper is available. `<resource-root>` is the skill's `resources` directory or the agent resource directory containing `capability.json`. The loader must emit the full selected payload; but a filename, search result, hash, truncated excerpt, or self-authored \"read\" receipt is not delivery evidence. Supply each subagent the complete relevant resources and preserve tool or host delivery evidence.",
            "kind": "guarded_invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-meta-supercharge:L213:01bab8d26727",
            "heading": "Resource Delivery Gate",
            "source": "ssot/engos-meta-supercharge.md",
            "source_line": 222,
            "sha256": "01bab8d2672760842d0a6f540634b25f3504968a7940276be5a243b2deb053d6",
            "text": "If a required resource is missing, stale, changed during execution, or incompletely delivered, recover it before dependent work. Do not guess its contents or silently shorten the route. Delivery does not prove comprehension; independent checks must use behavior that depends on the resource. Do not claim host enforcement unless a verified host actually supplies it.",
            "kind": "guarded_invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-meta-supercharge:L218:2c2a3cd3d571",
            "heading": "Resource Delivery Failure (Fail Closed)",
            "source": "ssot/engos-meta-supercharge.md",
            "source_line": 227,
            "sha256": "2c2a3cd3d57153892d544391edc59cda90e526955ecccfa6d1696bb4d257339a",
            "text": "- do not claim that the route is unsupported",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-meta-supercharge:L219:6c7c3fc931a0",
            "heading": "Resource Delivery Failure (Fail Closed)",
            "source": "ssot/engos-meta-supercharge.md",
            "source_line": 228,
            "sha256": "6c7c3fc931a09bd50661b58e0b4bdacfc021616f24c8e2cdac239c133f7058c3",
            "text": "- do not substitute a generic response, a shortened route, or another module",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-meta-supercharge:L220:3d574abfbdc7",
            "heading": "Resource Delivery Failure (Fail Closed)",
            "source": "ssot/engos-meta-supercharge.md",
            "source_line": 229,
            "sha256": "3d574abfbdc7e45dcd3cf8aa317e1d124b3f2f81f83a0d06c5fc1ed4e1c01dc7",
            "text": "- do not execute the requested route until the resource is recovered and rechecked",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-meta-supercharge:L223:4c695efce4a9",
            "heading": "Output Precedence",
            "source": "ssot/engos-meta-supercharge.md",
            "source_line": 232,
            "sha256": "4c695efce4a93f80586c41a7222a97f652812bddd20a0e9489bfdf744ff8ba54",
            "text": "Terminal help/examples/details and `/gaslight list` or `/gaslight help` return only their specified output. `/catchup` retains its exact tables and validation text, without generic wrapper sections. `/contract` retains `Contract Spec` and its exact QA JSON schema; when the user explicitly requests JSON-only, return only that JSON with missing context or gaps represented in its existing fields. Other stacks retain canonical pass order and module output shapes under the general wrapper; `/full` supplies its own pass wrappers. `/ult /full` does not execute the generated task and says so explicitly. No precedence rule permits fabricated results or skipping independent review.",
            "kind": "guarded_invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-meta-supercharge:L231:1f2f66d251cf",
            "heading": "HARD CONSTRAINTS",
            "source": "ssot/engos-meta-supercharge.md",
            "source_line": 240,
            "sha256": "1f2f66d251cf2341cfc491f9858cf5894c47d33e810a06a3d1c77e3e3284b4ce",
            "text": "- Only run capstone when a deliverable is complete or the user says done, ship, or finish.",
            "kind": "guarded_invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-meta-supercharge:L232:0f7011d4f632",
            "heading": "HARD CONSTRAINTS",
            "source": "ssot/engos-meta-supercharge.md",
            "source_line": 241,
            "sha256": "0f7011d4f63204ffbe768e8ca1563c9c913aaa43b10d7b02b88e54f85e37be3f",
            "text": "- Do not run capstone after small replies.",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-meta-supercharge:L234:811378a9f2b4",
            "heading": "HARD CONSTRAINTS",
            "source": "ssot/engos-meta-supercharge.md",
            "source_line": 243,
            "sha256": "811378a9f2b4cead606e14ff92a39523941643cb6b2fc9e91636c264d9de7ef0",
            "text": "- The capstone uses the `/catchup` resource-delivery gate. If that route cannot be loaded, report the delivery block and do not append an improvised or generic catch-up.",
            "kind": "guarded_invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-meta-supercharge:L237:bf84a9ca15a8",
            "heading": "HELP OUTPUT (Quick Guide)",
            "source": "ssot/engos-meta-supercharge.md",
            "source_line": 246,
            "sha256": "bf84a9ca15a8049a88b6c106a56714ead4283e4e414046ba35c5e9a4d79d9a96",
            "text": "For a terminal help request, load route `help` from the resource map and read `resources/references/help.md` and return its help content only. Do not execute its examples or continue into an operational module.",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-meta-supercharge:L240:bd45ef1c4189",
            "heading": "HELP EXAMPLES OUTPUT (Auto-Generated Examples)",
            "source": "ssot/engos-meta-supercharge.md",
            "source_line": 249,
            "sha256": "bd45ef1c4189a860f61d205742bac16d6b82f46864747e88ce7eca12b7585427",
            "text": "For a terminal help-examples request, load route `examples` and read `resources/references/help-examples.md` and follow its exact example-generation and output contract. Do not execute the examples.",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-meta-supercharge:L242:bc6e78faf2d2",
            "heading": "HELP EXAMPLES OUTPUT (Auto-Generated Examples)",
            "source": "ssot/engos-meta-supercharge.md",
            "source_line": 251,
            "sha256": "bc6e78faf2d2f8a6f485af354eff43935a788e688825b2e17fdfd55c77156d0d",
            "text": "For a skill surface, these paths are relative to the skill directory. For an agent surface, resolve `references/help.md` and `references/help-examples.md` relative to the directory containing its bundled `capability.json`. If a required help resource is unavailable, report the missing resource instead of inventing or silently shortening the help contract.",
            "kind": "guarded_invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-meta-supercharge:L245:1086282a839e",
