        "protected_invariants": [
          {
            "id": "engos-meta-uac-import:L22:f0d947235149",
            "heading": "Purpose",
            "source": "ssot/engos-meta-uac-import.md",
            "source_line": 29,
            "sha256": "f0d947235149d1f776768e53d1bf7eedf6a3f1c185fe10202d102117f85900ec",
            "text": "Deterministic clarity lint from `instruction_clarity.v1` is available in every mode and enabled by default for `audit`, `plan`, and `judge`. It is advisory and never counts as behavioral evidence.",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-meta-uac-import:L25:9581f6c1acb5",
            "heading": "Primary Objective",
            "source": "ssot/engos-meta-uac-import.md",
            "source_line": 32,
            "sha256": "9581f6c1acb5533bc007bfd7bf29a4a37f716f9428b4aac23fc52a85873b6eff",
            "text": "Improve the supplied skill or agent\u2019s clarity, completeness, coherence, structure, and usability while preserving its intended capability and existing surface kind and provider scope. Classify safely, recommend the right surfaces, and refuse landing until the structural and reviewed requirement gates pass. Structural diagnostics do not prove downstream model efficacy.",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-meta-uac-import:L44:83466994e31c",
            "heading": "Invocation Contract",
            "source": "ssot/engos-meta-uac-import.md",
            "source_line": 51,
            "sha256": "83466994e31cb2c5e6568d5df77cc763081ee051e50abf72e348e72013992fb1",
            "text": "- deploy is separate and must never be implied by `apply`",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-meta-uac-import:L45:0246bb0452fe",
            "heading": "Invocation Contract",
            "source": "ssot/engos-meta-uac-import.md",
            "source_line": 52,
            "sha256": "0246bb0452fe016af5e26128122b13e5ef8d943ff6ccd5b437ec5bc65ecf7a89",
            "text": "- when shell entrypoints are required to complete the workflow, say so explicitly instead of assuming the caller knows them",
            "kind": "guarded_invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-meta-uac-import:L51:e22510630d6f",
            "heading": "Output Directory",
            "source": "ssot/engos-meta-uac-import.md",
            "source_line": 58,
            "sha256": "e22510630d6f328dddd3035251d13d56bc2d43006fa3f3f6d5e6af8460d4850a",
            "text": "Canonical application writes `ssot/<slug>.md` and `.meta/capabilities/<slug>.json`, plus generated surfaces and evaluation contracts. Quality review evidence belongs in `reports/quality-reviews/<slug>/`; baseline lineage lives in `sources/ssot-baselines/<slug>/` and changes only under the independent promotion policy. These are UAC-owned onboarding artifacts, not output paths imposed on the imported capability's own task.",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-meta-uac-import:L60:962b6e33d082",
            "heading": "Workflow",
            "source": "ssot/engos-meta-uac-import.md",
            "source_line": 67,
            "sha256": "962b6e33d082ac1735fd57b138d61fe9c7f311ccb55a5f5e53fb19fa60c0c268",
            "text": "7. Classify reusable workflows as `skill` by default. Agent-related headings, quoted examples, and independent-review requirements do not justify a named agent. Route undeclared native-agent configuration to `manual_review`; preserve existing explicit `agent` or `both` declarations until a reviewed surface change. New or expanded agent emission requires the user's explicit approval for the capability and each provider, plus a hash-bound independent UAC requirement review explaining the execution need. A general improvement request, reviewer verdict, score, or `--yes` does not grant creation approval. Record the actual user approval reference and scoped identities in the existing review's `user_approval` field; never synthesize approval from an inferred preference. Preserve an existing approval reference when improving the same approved registration; ask only for genuinely new identities.",
            "kind": "guarded_invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-meta-uac-import:L64:63afafdd71cc",
            "heading": "Workflow",
            "source": "ssot/engos-meta-uac-import.md",
            "source_line": 71,
            "sha256": "63afafdd71cc6cdcf95ef2a1cbc255b7841377f88479f27209f457262a84a2e1",
            "text": "11. On `judge`, do not land or modify canonical repository state. Mechanical repairs produce a candidate artifact only. Inspect structure, formatting, style, ambiguity, contradictions, missing details, references, outputs, boundaries, and preservation. Return an explicit disposition for each applicable dimension. Apply only targeted mechanical repairs; request source-grounded semantic repairs from the invoking agent and an independent reviewer when meaning is unresolved. Do not append generic obligations to satisfy a count.",
            "kind": "guarded_invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-meta-uac-import:L66:4d6263b78413",
            "heading": "Workflow",
            "source": "ssot/engos-meta-uac-import.md",
            "source_line": 73,
            "sha256": "4d6263b784139fcdeeeddd1cd03f337fc233055c2de3a8137c9e2a0c287ec390",
            "text": "13. Search for benchmark sources only when the source is generic or fit confidence is weak.",
            "kind": "guarded_invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-meta-uac-import:L67:508b32565297",
            "heading": "Workflow",
            "source": "ssot/engos-meta-uac-import.md",
            "source_line": 74,
            "sha256": "508b32565297a9501887f58024f855d563b375c159cece377080ea9830e29d10",
            "text": "14. Report `structural_ready` only for structural checks. Keep semantic review attestations, assembled resource content, host delivery evidence, and measured behavioral results distinct. No average score can waive an unresolved blocker.",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-meta-uac-import:L69:082360db6cc5",
            "heading": "Workflow",
            "source": "ssot/engos-meta-uac-import.md",
            "source_line": 76,
            "sha256": "082360db6cc59590c03f5d502f1aeb2e5311ecf003058abf6c6a13a0f480a535",
            "text": "16. On `apply`, refuse landing unless the quality loop reaches `structural_ready`. Validate any supplied `PromotionVerdict.v2`; reject stale hashes or a mismatched slug. Treat `PromotionVerdict.v1` as read-only legacy evidence that cannot authorize promotion. During advisory rollout, an absent verdict leaves the result `behavioral_pending` and cannot materialize a new behavioral baseline.",
            "kind": "guarded_invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
          {
            "id": "engos-meta-uac-import:L70:06b1f12c679f",
            "heading": "Workflow",
            "source": "ssot/engos-meta-uac-import.md",
            "source_line": 77,
            "sha256": "06b1f12c679f67ed361af6fdb25665d53b26aba09ae4ec8982ee817c378940ea",
            "text": "17. On authorized `apply`, write canonical SSOT and the descriptor, persist the quality reviews, then rebuild and validate generated surfaces. Materialize a new baseline only after an independent `promote` verdict, or preserve a valid historical baseline without rewriting its lineage.",
            "kind": "invariant",
            "mapped_to": []
          },
